+1

Clock skew / short token TTL

If tokens are very short lived or the clock on the pod is skewed, the token may be considered expired by the broker, causing the handshake to fail and the client to eventually time out.

TLS / SNI / ALPN / cipher mismatch causing the SASL frame not to be processed

Less likely since you said TCP conn succeeds — but still possible the TLS is accepted but broker discards handshake because of misconfigured certs or ALPN. Check broker TLS logs if possible.

IAM role / Workload Identity permission missing for token exchange

You mentioned the SA has roles/managedkafka.client and roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator — double-check the exact role bindings, Workload Identity pool binding, and token audience used when fetching the token.